//? Title: Gapped insertion in the library-sort API
//? Subtitle: Actual shelf states, original deterministic values and quadratic shift controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Gaps can make an insertion cheap, but their presence alone does not establish
the published randomized library-sort bound. The current API uses a
deterministic fixed shelf of2*n+2 slots. We inspect its actual predecessor/gap
decisions and shelf snapshots, retain the original40-value fixture, and measure
the descending-input quadratic shift pattern. No random arrival-order assumption
or fictional rebalance history is introduced.
)

\toc

> The implemented shelf invariant

The occupied values appear in ascending order when gaps are skipped. Place the
first input at shelf midpoint n+1, then find the rightmost occupied value not
exceeding the new value. Its following slot is the desired position. If empty,
fill it. Otherwise find the first empty slot to its right, shift the intervening
occupied run right by one, then place the new value. This preserves sorted order
and the exact input multiplicities. Zero is a valid value, so occupancy is a
separate flag rather than a sentinel.

The old implementation reserved2*n+2 slots from the start. Its rebalance
condition2*(m+1)>capacity could never hold because m+1<=n. Its left-shift
fallback was also unreachable: after k insertions the largest occupied slot is
at most n+k<=2*n, leaving slot2*n+1 empty. The checked producer retains the
reachable historical behavior and records only real seed, direct and right-shift
placements. No randomized insertion order or geometric rebalance schedule
implements the paper’s expected bound here.

> A tiny actual right shift

Insert4,3,2. The first4 goes at midpoint4 of an eight-slot shelf. Then3 occupies
slot0. Inserting2 targets occupied slot0, moves3 into the actual gap at slot1,
and writes2 at slot0. The diagram shows just these two relevant slots before and
after the real third insertion; the table prints every actual shelf slot,
including the unchanged midpoint4.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/library_sort_shift.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/library_sort.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::library_sort_trace({4, 3, 2});
    auto e = t.insertions.back();
    auto before = t.shelves[2], after = t.shelves[3];
    std::print("| actual slot | actual before occupied | actual before value, ignore if gap | actual after " "occupied | actual after value, ignore if gap |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | --- | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t j = 0; j < before.slots.size(); ++j)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", j, bool(before.occupied[j]),
                   before.slots[j], bool(after.occupied[j]), after.slots[j]);
    std::print("\nActual original input index {}; value {}; target {}; original gap {}; moved slot pairs " "{}.\n",
               e.input_index, e.value, e.target, e.gap, e.moved);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("old0", {0, 2},
           std::format("Actual before slot0\noccupied{}; value{}",
                       bool(before.occupied[0]), before.slots[0])).node(
        "old1", {6, 2}, "Actual before slot1\nempty gap").node(
        "new0", {0, -2},
        std::format("Actual after slot0\nnew input{}", after.slots[0])).node(
        "new1", {6, -2},
        std::format("Actual after slot1\nmoved value{}", after.slots[1])).edge(
        "old0", "new1", "actual right shift");
    d.save_svg("build/library_sort_shift.svg");
}
```
