> A measured quadratic shift family

For strictly descending n inputs, after the midpoint seed the second value goes
directly into slot0. Every subsequent smaller value shifts the occupied low-end
run right. The exact number of moved slot pairs is

$$\sum_{j=1}^{n-2}j=(n-1)(n-2)/2.$$
\alttext(Descending arrival order produces a triangular quadratic number of actual shelf shifts.)

Ascending arrival order uses direct placements after the midpoint and moves zero
slot pairs, though gap-skipping predecessor searches still perform real work.
Thus neither shift count alone nor the existence of unused space gives an
expected O(n log n) theorem. The next plot compares actual measured shifts with
the explicitly labelled descending formula, using complete count-only native
runs rather than a timing proxy or repeated-prefix history.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/library_sort_quadratic.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/library_sort.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <numeric>
#include <algorithm>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, y, reference;
    std::print("| original length | actual descending moved pairs | exact descending formula | actual " "ascending moved pairs |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (int n : {4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256}) {
        std::vector<int> a(n);
        std::iota(a.begin(), a.end(), 0);
        auto ascending = dm::algorithms::library_sort_analyze(a);
        std::reverse(a.begin(), a.end());
        auto descending = dm::algorithms::library_sort_analyze(a);
        const auto formula = std::size_t(n - 1) * (n - 2) / 2;
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, descending.work.shift_writes,
                   formula, ascending.work.shift_writes);
        x.push_back(n);
        y.push_back(descending.work.shift_writes);
        reference.push_back(formula);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, reference, "exact descending formula", {22, 163, 74}, 1.5).points(
        x, y, "actual descending shifts", {37, 99, 235}, 5).y_limits(0, 45000).title("Actual quadratic shifts on descending input").x_label("original input length").y_label("occupied slot pairs moved").save_svg("build/library_sort_quadratic.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| original length | actual descending moved pairs | exact descending formula | actual ascending moved pairs |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 4 | 3 | 3 | 0 |
| 8 | 21 | 21 | 0 |
| 16 | 105 | 105 | 0 |
| 32 | 465 | 465 | 0 |
| 64 | 1953 | 1953 | 0 |
| 128 | 8001 | 8001 | 0 |
| 256 | 32385 | 32385 | 0 |
\image(figures/library_sort_quadratic.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual descending shifts against the exact triangular-count formula.)
\alttext(Measured native work and the separately identified formula coincide; ascending controls demonstrate that shift cost depends strongly on arrival order.)

> Value comparisons are only part of the work

The predecessor search skips empty flags while narrowing an index range. One
occupied value comparison can therefore hide many occupancy reads. Counters
separate real search iterations, value comparisons, occupancy decisions and
moved slot pairs; final output scans every fixed shelf slot. These counts
exclude guards, allocation/copies, capture and elapsed time. A conservative
gap-scan bound is O(n^2*log(n+1)) time with O(n) runtime shelf storage, while
the observed descending shift lower bound already rules out a universal O(n log
n) total-work guarantee for this implementation. No tight worst-case search
theorem is inferred from the four finite controls.

For64 values, compare increasing, decreasing, all-equal and the explicit LCG
fixture. The panels keep value comparisons distinct from occupancy reads. All
are actual counts from one complete native run per input, and no unused
rebalance or left-shift events are invented.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/library_sort_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/library_sort.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <numeric>
#include <algorithm>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<int> ascending(64);
    std::iota(ascending.begin(), ascending.end(), 0);
    auto descending = ascending;
    std::reverse(descending.begin(), descending.end());
    std::vector<std::vector<int>> inputs{ascending, descending,
                                         std::vector<int>(64, 0),
                                         dm::algorithms::library_sort_demo_input(64)};
    std::vector<std::string> labels{"increasing", "decreasing", "all equal",
                                    "LCG fixture"};
    std::vector<double> x, comparisons, reads;
    std::print("| explicit original control | actual value comparisons | actual occupancy reads | actual " "shifted pairs | actual full output slots |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < inputs.size(); ++i) {
        auto a = dm::algorithms::library_sort_analyze(inputs[i]);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", labels[i],
                   a.work.comparisons, a.work.occupancy_reads,
                   a.work.shift_writes, a.work.output_slots);
        x.push_back(i);
        comparisons.push_back(a.work.comparisons);
        reads.push_back(a.work.occupancy_reads);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), q = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, comparisons, "actual comparisons", {37, 99, 235}, 6).title(
        "Actual occupied-value comparisons").x_label("listed input control index").y_label("value comparisons");
    q.points(x, reads, "actual reads", {220, 38, 38}, 6).title(
        "Actual predecessor/gap occupancy tests").x_label(
        "listed input control index").y_label("occupancy flag reads");
    dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2, 1).add(p).add(q).size(900, 800).title(
        "Actual work components on64-value controls").fit_panels().save_svg(
        "build/library_sort_work.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| explicit original control | actual value comparisons | actual occupancy reads | actual shifted pairs | actual full output slots |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| increasing | 115 | 7035 | 0 | 130 |
| decreasing | 316 | 4568 | 1953 | 130 |
| all equal | 115 | 7035 | 0 | 130 |
| LCG fixture | 305 | 4602 | 535 | 130 |
\image(figures/library_sort_work.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual comparison and occupancy work on four explicit arrival patterns.)
\alttext(Separate native counters show gap-skipping cost that a value-comparison count omits; no wall-clock performance or randomized complexity is claimed.)

> Contracts and verification

Arbitrary int values and duplicates are valid. Empty/one-element inputs use the
historical trivial-copy branch without allocating a shelf or claiming gapped
placements. Complete signed predecessor,2*n+2 shelf and container geometry is
checked before the algorithm. The legacy by-value API can copy its input before
body guards; the analysis/trace APIs borrow input and return owned results. The
guaranteed unused right tail makes a missing-right-gap internal error
unreachable on admitted valid geometry.

For n>=2, exact complete trace admission counts n original values, n insertion
records and(n+1)*(1+2*(2*n+2)) shelf/slot/flag records. Trivial inputs capture
only their n original values. The million-record cap is checked before copies or
sorting and excludes scalar fields, capacities/result/runtime copies and
bytes/RAM;0 disables only the optional cap. Every actual shelf and placement is
owned and comes from one producing execution.

Native tests exhaust permutations through length seven and ternary words through
length six, compare every occupied shelf with its sorted input prefix, and
verify real shifts, gaps, work counts, guards and ownership. The ten-report
batch passed 101 native CTest cases, 34 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan cases,
103 compiled/executed public examples, 515/515 scoped file definitions plus 10
exact LCG class definitions, and ten representative clangd hovers. Independent
Python integer/Fraction, explicit-label graph search, quadratic sequence DP and
full weighted-stump references passed 69430 records across all ten topics,
including a separately fitted held-out Iris model. Frozen ordinary compatibility
passed 1000 Lex-BFS orders, 1000 library sorts, 100 LBG codebooks, 100 complete
five-round LogitBoost ensembles and 200 LLL bases; corrected LBG final
labels/objectives are intentionally excluded from historical compatibility. All
4 complete programs executed and all 4 native figures were rendered and visually
reviewed, with clipped legends corrected and rerun. HTML/Markdown
computed-result and figure-byte checks gate legacy retirement. Repeatable
receipts are retained in `build/mepml-conversion/batch-204-213/`.

> References

M. A. Bender, M. Farach-Colton and M. A. Mosteiro(2006),
[Insertion Sort is O(n log n)|https://doi.org/10.1007/s00224-005-1237-z], Theory
of Computing Systems39(3),391–397. The name motivates the use of gaps; this
historical deterministic fixed-capacity variant explicitly does not implement
the paper’s randomized insertion/rebalance assumptions or inherit its guarantee.
